IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`

-- wra3-pt4-s95.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, section 95 (interpretation of Part 4).
-- Part wra3, layer 1. Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk (version 2026-07-01),
-- not the official text. Every definition is encoded as a table or function with a test (wra3-tests-pt4-s95.l4).
-- "means" is a closed definition: a thing outside it is JUST FALSE. Where a definition points at regulations ("prescribed")
-- the answer is NOTHING unless the regulations' answer is supplied.

§ `s 95 Interpretation of Part 4`

-- The four Scottish disability payments that section 95 defines and section 77(4) names.
-- The declared type and its constructors carry the section label so that no other part can declare the same name.
-- src:1510 | In this Part—
-- src:1511 | “adult disability payment” means disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022;
-- src:1512 | “child disability payment” means disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 (S.S.I. 2021/174);
-- src:1513 | “daily living activities” has the meaning given by section 78(4);
-- src:1514 | “daily living component” means the daily living component of personal independence payment;
-- src:1515 | “mobility activities” has the meaning given by section 79(4);
-- src:1516 | “mobility component” means the mobility component of personal independence payment;
-- src:1517 | “pension age disability payment” means disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024;
-- src:1518 | “prescribed” means prescribed by regulations;
-- src:1519 | “Scottish adult disability living allowance” means disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025.
@ref s 95 (src:1510-1519)
DECLARE `s 95 Scottish disability assistance` IS ONE OF
    `s 95 Scottish adult disability living allowance`
    `s 95 pension age disability payment`
    `s 95 adult disability payment`
    `s 95 child disability payment`

-- "adult disability payment" means disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for
-- Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022; and likewise for the other three. The title is a STRING because the
-- regulations are not among the sources.
@ref s 95 "adult disability payment", "child disability payment", "pension age disability payment", "Scottish adult disability living allowance" (src:1511-1512)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `s 95 Scottish disability assistance`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 95 disability assistance given in accordance with` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `s 95 adult disability payment`                    THEN "Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022"
    WHEN `s 95 child disability payment`                    THEN "Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 (S.S.I. 2021/174)"
    WHEN `s 95 pension age disability payment`              THEN "Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024"
    WHEN `s 95 Scottish adult disability living allowance`  THEN "Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025"

-- Is the disability assistance a person receives the named payment? It is if it is given in accordance with the named
-- regulations, and not otherwise.
@ref s 95 "adult disability payment", "child disability payment", "pension age disability payment", "Scottish adult disability living allowance" (src:1511-1512)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `s 95 Scottish disability assistance`
      `the regulations the disability assistance is given in accordance with` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95 the disability assistance is the payment named` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 95 disability assistance given in accordance with` `the payment` EQUALS `the regulations the disability assistance is given in accordance with`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means disability assistance given in accordance with" the named regulations (a closed definition)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 95 "daily living component" (src:1514)
`s 95 daily living component means the daily living component of personal independence payment` MEANS `daily living component`

@ref s 95 "mobility component" (src:1516)
`s 95 mobility component means the mobility component of personal independence payment` MEANS `mobility component`

-- "daily living activities" has the meaning given by section 78(4); "mobility activities" by section 79(4).
-- The meaning is those sections' own, so the answer here is the section that gives it.
@ref s 95 "daily living activities" (src:1513)
`s 95 daily living activities has the meaning given by` MEANS "section 78(4)"

@ref s 95 "mobility activities" (src:1515)
`s 95 mobility activities has the meaning given by` MEANS "section 79(4)"

-- "prescribed" means prescribed by regulations. The regulations are not among the sources, so the matter is prescribed
-- only if the caller supplies that regulations prescribe it.
@ref s 95 "prescribed" (src:1518)
GIVEN `regulations made under Part 4 prescribe the matter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95 the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations made under Part 4 prescribe the matter`
    WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed” means prescribed by regulations" (a closed definition)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING
